\DOC VAL_INT64_TAC

\TYPE {VAL_INT64_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Given a numeral-valued term {t}, adds the assumption {val (word t) = t} to the
goal, leaving the conclusion unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {t : term} is the natural-number term whose 64-bit word encoding
is asserted to round-trip through {val}; the new assumption is built from
exactly this term. The conclusion is untouched and all existing assumptions are
kept, with the new assumption appended at the end of the assumption list:
{
           A ?- u
   =============================  VAL_INT64_TAC t
      A, val (word t) = t ?- u
}
\noindent The tactic discharges the justification of the new assumption itself,
so no extra subgoal is produced for it. The term {t} may be a variable or a
compound arithmetic expression.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of outcome, always on goals that
already carry assumptions bounding the relevant quantities.

\ENDDOC
